      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I second this. And would also add contacts that require fingers and hands to this. I like making avatar interaction systems but most of them require the use of hands to hit buttons on contacts or manipulate physbones. An alternate API that can be added to avatars that activates certain things with specific key presses or highlighting objects similar to interacting with stations or picking up objects in world would go a long way in improving this. \n\nNot to mention increasing the ability for the eventual mobile phone users.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-09T20:10:45.128Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The SDK already allows for posing PhysBones in the game view, so applying that same logic to the Desktop client would't be much of a stretch.\n\nI would think adding it to when a player holds TAB, which unlocks the mouse cursor, would be an easy and unobtrusive way of adding it into the game. Obviously would need to have a falloff so desktop users can't pose bones miles away.\n\nnakos",
